urich Witellikerstrasse 40, CH-8008 Zürich, Switzerland. Christian Wolpert, Department of Medicine-Cardiology, Nephrology and Internal Intensive Care Medicine Posilipostr. 4, 71640 Ludwigsburg, Germany. Supplementary material Supplementary material is available at Europace online. Funding No funding was received for this article. Data availability Not applicable. References 1. Raatikainen MJP, Arnar DO, Merkely B, Nielsen JC, Hindricks G, Heidbuchel H, et al. A decade of information on the use of cardiac implantable electronic devices and interventional electrophysiological procedures in the European Society of Cardiology Countries: 2017 report from the European Heart Rhythm Association. Europace 2017;19:ii1–90. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 2. Merino JL, Arribas F, Botto GL, Huikuri H, Kraemer LI, Linde C, et al. Core curriculum for the heart rhythm specialist. Europace 2009;11:iii1–26. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 3. Tzeis S, Theuns DA, Earley M, Merino JL, Leclercq C. EHRA certification: a 15-year journey of attesting excellence in arrhythmia healthcare. Europace 2022;24:175–8. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 4. EHRA Certification Web Page. https://www.escardio.org/Education/Career-Development/Certification/EHRA-Certification (7 December 2023, date last accessed). 5. Defaye P, Biffi M, El-Chami M, Boveda S, Glikson M, Piccini J, et al. Cardiac pacing and lead devices management: 25 years of research at EP Europace journal. Europace 2023;25:euad202. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 6. Paul T, Krause U, Sanatani S, Etheridge SP. Advancing the science of management of arrhythmic disease in children and adult congenital heart disease patients within the last 25 years. Europace 2023;25:euad155. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 7. Svennberg E, Caiani EG, Bruining N, Desteghe L, Han JK, Narayan SM, et al. The digital journey: 25 years of digital development in electrophysiology from an Europace p